Negative control for filter-wire.test.ts.

Collapses the toggle group's falsy member to the unset one, so choosing "no" on a
tri-state writes `null` and the translator emits the same empty string an
untouched column emits — "show me the ones that did NOT bounce" silently becomes
"show me everything". Any assertion that reads the wire value of a `false`
column, or keeps a set column apart from an unset one, goes red; one that reads
only the `true` position stays green.

